Subject: [PATCH] CPU-features CF0: measured baseline for the CPU feature
 contract (docs)

Post-UPKEEP audit with every prior plan closed and upstream main
(957c12c) tree-identical to this branch. The next block is chosen by
measurement, north-star first: the advertised-vs-implemented CPU
matrix in docs/plans/CPU_FEATURES_PLAN.md finds the CR4.SMEP/SMAP
walk guards inverted since the original upstream code (harness
repro: with SMEP on, CPL0 faults fetching its own supervisor text
and freely executes a user page; invisible today only because
CPUID advertises neither feature and no test ever vectored them),
four capabilities that work but read 0 in CPUID (NX, SYSCALL,
1 GiB pages, CLFLUSH), IA32_PAT as sparse storage with a 0 reset
value where the SDM default is 0x0007040600070406, and PCID absent
while AuraLite-OS (74c2b9b, its HW_PLAN H4) carries a full PCID
runtime that no QEMU configuration can execute -- this emulator
can become its first lane. An MSR census over the firmware and
both SeaBIOS ISO lanes bounds the validation question. Defect
ledger D1-D6, five decisions (advertise-nothing-until-pinned at
the front), phases CF1-CF5, and a ranked device backlog (modern
virtio first) for the choice after this plan.

Doc-sync in the same commit: STATUS "Current limits" no longer
contradicts PM P0-P3 or UPKEEP U3; ROADMAP gains the missing
PM/UPKEEP ledger rows, the CPU_FEATURES row, gap row 5 and the
refreshed upstream (957c12c) inventory. Docs only; make test
green with both live SeaBIOS ISO lanes on this tree.
